    "aggregation": "Common-workload aggregates exclude setup and the four Warm-only workloads. They are arithmetic sums of seven operations, not medians or latency distributions.",
    "baseline": "Prepared whole-object zstd and raw use the same authenticated transfer protocol and cache-aware receiver. They already avoid sending remaining prepared frames when an identical object is present.",
    "bytes": "Logical encrypted-stream bytes count both directions, canonical envelopes and frame prefixes. Two-guest physical stream bytes count both verified relay hops. They exclude virtio headers/control/credits, VM boot assets and stored verification fixtures.",
    "time": "encode_through_publication_us is sender operation wall time through authenticated publication reply. sender_exchange_wall_us includes canonical authorization/crypto, send/wait/receive, remote processing and reply; it is not pure link send time.",
    "cpu": "sender_reported_cpu_us and receiver_processing_cpu_us remain separate; the receiver timer excludes framed receive/allocation/copy. Their sum is a limited reported quantity across differing guest/host accounting domains. Host OS worker/orchestrator lifecycle CPU is separate and must not be added to nested guest CPU.",
    "statistical_scope": "One trial per cell, fixed registered order, synthetic public fixtures and local HVF; no WAN, median/p95, physical-energy or stable performance-superiority claim."
  },
