  "interpretation": [
    "All recorded accepted transfers preserved exact bytes and original length through stopped-store readback; all two-guest objects also passed keyless read-only reboot verification.",
    "The seven matched workload sums show about 65.76%-66.62% fewer logical encrypted bytes and 2.40x-3.03x lower summed operation wall time for Warm versus Whole in these four single-trial cells.",
    "Identical repeats lose to Whole in all four cells: Warm uses slightly more encrypted bytes and more operation wall time and reported CPU. The baseline already deduplicates repeats; it is not a full raw resend.",
    "Localized edits show substantial conditional savings, including the two-guest 16 MiB case at 25,497 logical bytes and 233,752 us versus Whole at 32,153,825 bytes and 6,921,060 us. Both physical paths multiply these byte counts by two.",
    "Unrelated-object outcomes are mixed: 1 MiB Warm is slower than Whole, while 16 MiB wall time is close; this pilot does not establish a universal speedup.",
    "The four Warm-only schema/runtime operations total 119,159-120,077 logical bytes for 94,710 reconstructed bytes. Individual generated/residual operations are smaller than their objects, but setup and a matched conventional baseline are required before any runtime-specific performance claim.",
    "The actual local MVM integration works. This pilot does not establish WAN performance, complete endpoint CPU savings, energy savings, a production mailbox or host-compromise confidentiality."
  ]
